# Packages

Every package this hql knows: the builtin packages the binary carries, and
the installable packages the package registry lists. The terms, builtin and
installable, official and known, internal and external, are the
[packages card](../wiki/hql/packages.hmd)'s. Checked on 2026-11-13 against
`lib/` of this repository and against `main` of
[hql-extensions](https://github.com/ewiger/hql-extensions).

## Builtin packages

Under `lib/`, one folder each: contracts bundled with the binary, extension
compiled in and internal. `src/extensions/mod.rs` registers one descriptor
per package, each with its `id`, `abi = 1` and `provides`.

| Package | Extension | Modules | Prelude | Contracts |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `std` | `std`, internal | 33: 28 provided by the extension, 5 by the runtime (`doc`, `retrieval`, `knowledge`, `vault`, `validators`) | yes, `lib/std/prelude.hql`, the implicit import list | [`lib/std/`](../../lib/std/README.md) |
| `search` | `search`, internal | 2, `lexical` and `semantic`, both provided by the extension | no; each module is imported where it is used | [`lib/search/`](../../lib/search/README.md) |

The modules `std`'s extension provides: `core`, `collections`, `string`,
`seq`, `math`, `stats`, `time`, `random`, `option`, `result`, `regex`,
`graph`, `format`, `io`, `io.net`, `io.logging`, `io.fs`, `io.env`,
`io.db.sqlite`, `io.db.postgres`, `io.db.spark`, `io.transaction`,
`io.msg.nats`, `io.msg.nats_jetstream`, `bytes`, `encoding`, `crypto`,
`crypto.digest`. What each module declares is stated in its package's
README, not here.

## Installable packages

Listed in `hql-packages.yaml` at the root of [hql-extensions](https://github.com/ewiger/hql-extensions). An official
package's crate lives under `crates/` of that repository; a known package's
crate lives elsewhere.

| Package | Kind | Crate | Version | hql | Provides | State |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `ml` | official | `hql-ext-ml` | 0.1.0 | `>=0.7.0, <0.8.0` | `ml`, `ml.metrics` | contracts and a prelude under `modules/`; the library implements none of them |

There are no known packages. Nothing is installed anywhere: `hql` has no
`package` command, no `[packages]` table, nothing under `~/.hql/lib/`, and
no `hql::ext` API a crate can implement an extension against
([HQL-0057 part 1](../proposals/HQL-0057/parts/01-packages.md), "Current
state"). No release publishes prebuilt libraries
([part 3](../proposals/HQL-0057/parts/03-prebuilt-libraries.md)).
